# A callable launched over data it was given finds a name of its code in that data before a free input (plan M11 5a,
# the executor's reading B4): x is no place of f, D has it, and the write of y is published into D.
# Plan M11 5v: the declarations of ordinary Structures live in the data part of main; the root holds places and the call main().
# The fields of D, which the dump of D showed, are the places d_x and d_y of the root.
sub: f () (int: y 0)
    y := x + 1
sub: main () (
    D:
        int: x 5
        int: y 0
)
    call: D f
main()
int: seen main\data\D\y
int: d_x main\data\D\x
int: d_y main\data\D\y
